## 1. Executive summary

The full suite runs **712 tests** and finishes with **3 failures**. Two of the failures reproduce in isolation (one stale test assertion, one over-strict rate limit); the third is cross-test pollution from a module-level email thread pool.

The highest-risk verified issues are:

1. **DEBUG=True and a Django-generated `SECRET_KEY` in the shipped `.env`**, plus missing production transport hardening (`check --deploy` warnings W004/W008/W009/W012/W016/W018).
2. **Shared cache is effectively disabled** (`LocMemCache` fallback because `use_redis` is absent) and Redis failures are configured to be ignored, so every Gunicorn worker has its own rate-limit state.
3. **CSP report URL reflects the untrusted `Host` header** under a wildcard `ALLOWED_HOSTS` entry, allowing CSP telemetry to be redirected to an attacker-controlled subdomain.
4. **The create-superuser backdoor is still routed at `/sy/_admin/<email>/<password>/<secret>/`**, logs the submitted plaintext password, and emails every superuser on each log call.
5. **`/health` returns 500 for any POST body** because raw bytes are converted to a dict.
6. **The new ad-click interceptor hijacks the placeholder “advertise with us” slide** (`/advertise/` and `mailto:`), so a fresh installation cannot reach its only advertising enquiry CTA.
7. **Maintenance mode is bypassed by the ads-subdomain middleware**, and static assets/health are blocked by the maintenance middleware itself.
8. **Auth GET throttle keys on `REMOTE_ADDR` behind Cloudflare/Render**, so all users share one bucket and any user can block auth pages for everyone.
9. **Django admin still offers a hard account purge** (`AUTHENTICATION/admin.py`), bypassing the off-grid-only delete path and leaving advert assets orphaned.
10. **Hibernation leaves cached story pages stale** and shows an invalid support address on the login hold.
11. **Four stored-XSS sinks** — three in frontend JS (new comments, analytics story titles, profile/admin JSON pagers) and one in server-rendered story tokens (`javascript:` URLs in `filel`/`btn`) — allow same-origin script execution, including in admin sessions.
12. **“Only me” archive files are public in Cloudinary**; the Django proxy guard does not protect direct storage URLs.

> Note: several “risk” items (notably the true-delete URL shape and logging the target password to `info_logger`) were explicit product decisions in the prior work scope. They are recorded in section 5 as accepted design risks, not re-litigated as accidental bugs.

