## 3. Verified findings

### 3.1 Security and configuration

#### BUG-001 — CRITICAL — Development DEBUG and generated secret are the shipped defaults
- **Location:** `.env:1,3` (`DJANGO_SECRET="django-insecure-…"`, `DEBUG = True`); `NoName/settings.py:16`; `NoName/settings.py:18-27`.
- **Evidence:** `check --deploy` reports W004 (no HSTS), W008 (no SSL redirect), W009 (weak/generated `SECRET_KEY`), W012/W016/W018. Debug-only cookie settings are active. The secret value is intentionally not reproduced in this log.
- **Impact:** If this `.env` is deployed, Django tracebacks, debug tooling and insecure cookies are exposed and sessions can be forged.
- **Fix:** Fail fast in production when `DEBUG` is true or `SECRET_KEY` starts with `django-insecure-`; set HSTS/SSL redirect/secure cookies from environment parsed as strict booleans; ship an example env with safe placeholders.

#### BUG-002 — HIGH — Shared cache disabled; Redis exceptions silently ignored
- **Location:** `NoName/settings.py:283-303`; `.env` has `redis_url` but no `use_redis`.
- **Evidence:** Runtime startup prints `i no use redis`; `CACHES["default"]` is `LocMemCache`. Redis branch sets `"IGNORE_EXCEPTIONS": True`.
- **Impact:** Rate limits, verification-code throttles, CSP dedupe, backdoor throttles and cache invalidation are per-process. With Gunicorn, clients can multiply every limit by the worker count; a Redis outage would also be silent.
- **Fix:** Require Redis in production, parse `use_redis` strictly, remove `IGNORE_EXCEPTIONS` (or log/alert on failure), and assert at startup that production is not using LocMem.

#### BUG-003 — HIGH — CSP `report-uri` reflects the request `Host`
- **Location:** `NoName/settings.py:96-116` (wildcard `.example.com` appended to `ALLOWED_HOSTS` for advert subdomains); `_.middleware.py:60-81` (report URL built with `request.build_absolute_uri(reverse("csp_report"))`).
- **Evidence:** Auditor probe with `Host: evil.example.com` produced `report-uri http://evil.example.com/csp-report/` and the matching `Reporting-Endpoints` header.
- **Impact:** Browser CSP violation reports (document URI, blocked source, inline script samples) can be exfiltrated to an attacker-controlled subdomain; the real report stream can be poisoned.
- **Fix:** Build the report endpoint from `canonical_origin()`/`About.domain`, never from the request host; restrict wildcard host acceptance at middleware level.

#### BUG-004 — HIGH — `/health` returns 500 for non-empty POST bodies
- **Location:** `NoName/urls.py:31-41`, specifically line 38 (`post = dict(request.body) or {}`).
- **Evidence:** `Client().get('/health')` → 200; `Client().post('/health', data={'x':'1'})` → 500 (`TypeError: cannot convert dictionary update sequence element #0 to a sequence`). Line 40 also logs GET/POST/form contents with malformed `%{get}` / `%{ip}` formatting.
- **Impact:** POST-based liveness checks fail; request body contents can leak into logs.
- **Fix:** Return a static JSON payload (optionally with the client IP); do not parse or log bodies. If body data is needed, parse JSON explicitly with a size cap.

#### BUG-005 — HIGH — Create-superuser backdoor is still exposed and logs plaintext passwords
- **Location:** `NoName/urls.py:71` (`path('sy/', include("_.urls"))`), `_/urls.py:7`, `_/views.py:28-59`.
- **Evidence:** `GET /sy/_admin/<email>/<password>/<secret>/` creates a superuser (`_.views.py:52`) and returns its serialized data (`:56`). `_.views.py:41-45` builds a dict containing the plaintext password and passes it to `superuser_logger`, which emails every active superuser (`_.views.py:63-105`). The email-keyed rate limit (`admin-create:{email}`) is bypassed by varying the email.
- **Impact:** Superuser creation by anyone who learns/leaks `SY_SECRET`; credential disclosure in logs; unauthenticated mail amplification and Resend quota exhaustion.
- **Fix:** Remove the endpoint entirely (or require an authenticated superuser session + CSRF + POST body). Never log or URL-encode passwords. Keep alerts out of the request path and aggregate them.

#### BUG-006 — HIGH — Auth GET throttle uses `REMOTE_ADDR` instead of the real client IP
- **Location:** `AUTHENTICATION/middleware.py:9-47` (key at lines 23-25).
- **Evidence:** With Cloudflare/Render in front, `REMOTE_ADDR` is the proxy address. Auditor probe: two clients with different `CF-Connecting-IP` values but the same `REMOTE_ADDR` share the 3-requests/4-second bucket.
- **Impact:** Unrelated users trip each other's `429`; one actor can keep all auth pages blocked.
- **Fix:** Use a trusted-proxy-aware IP resolver (only trust forwarded headers when the immediate peer is a known proxy) and a shared cache.

#### BUG-007 — HIGH — `get_client_ip()` trusts spoofable proxy headers
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/abstract.py:19-47`.
- **Evidence:** No validation that `REMOTE_ADDR` is a trusted proxy before accepting `CF-Connecting-IP` or the first `X-Forwarded-For` entry. `GET /health` with a forged `CF-Connecting-IP: 9.9.9.9` returns that value. `is_rate_limited()` (`abstract.py:193`) and session tracking (`AUTHENTICATION/middleware.py:143-153`) inherit it.
- **Impact:** Rate-limit bypass, forged audit/session IPs.
- **Fix:** Validate immediate peer against a trusted proxy list (or use `django-ipware`), validate/normalize IP literals.

#### BUG-008 — MEDIUM — Maintenance middleware ordering and fail-closed default
- **Location:** `NoName/settings.py:179-195` (`MaintenanceModeMiddleware` before WhiteNoise, and after `AdsSubdomainMiddleware`); `_.middleware.py:255-293` (`getattr(settings, "MAINTENANCE_MODE", "TRUE")` at line 261).
- **Evidence:** With `MAINTENANCE_MODE='TRUE'`, `/health` and `/static/ads.txt` both return 503. Ads-subdomain short-circuits (see BUG-012) never reach the maintenance middleware.
- **Impact:** Maintenance page cannot load its own CSS/JS; health checks cannot distinguish maintenance from outage; ads pages remain live during the outage.
- **Fix:** Put WhiteNoise before maintenance, exempt `/health` and static paths, default the setting to `"FALSE"`, add `Retry-After`, and place maintenance before `AdsSubdomainMiddleware`.

#### BUG-009 — MEDIUM — `.env` maintenance key name mismatch
- **Location:** `.env:7` (`maintenance_mode = "false"`); `NoName/settings.py:281` (`os.getenv('MAINTENANCE_MODE', "FALSE")`).
- **Impact:** On case-sensitive Linux the env value is ignored; operators cannot enable maintenance mode via the documented key.
- **Fix:** Read both spellings with strict boolean parsing and log the effective value.

#### BUG-010 — MEDIUM — `is_rate_limited(reset_timeout=True)` slides TTL and grows the timestamp list
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/abstract.py:181-220`, especially 206-215; callers include `HOME/views.py:1229` and `HOME/views.py:2418`.
- **Evidence:** Every call resets the cache TTL to the full window and appends to a list that is never pruned in this branch.
- **Impact:** Continued attempts keep a user locked out indefinitely and grow the cached value without bound. The `remaining_time` calculation also uses `max(elapsed, 1)`, so it can go negative.
- **Fix:** Prune old timestamps, set expiry from the oldest surviving attempt, and do not refresh TTL while blocked.

#### BUG-011 — MEDIUM — Unbounded background executors; DEBUG inconsistency in single-email sender
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/email_single.py:22-24` and `:114-128`; `SERVICE_INTERNAL/indexnow.py:20-28,84-87`; batch sender short-circuits at `email_batch.py:173-178,385-390`.
- **Evidence:** Module-level `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4)` with unbounded queues and no shutdown hook. `_dispatch_email()` still calls `resend.Emails.send()` in DEBUG (only the `from` address changes) while batch senders skip sending entirely.
- **Impact:** Memory growth and lost work on restart; tests/development can attempt real outbound email. Also the source of the full-suite mail mock pollution.
- **Fix:** Use a bounded task queue with a shutdown hook and move the DEBUG short-circuit into `_dispatch_email()`.

#### BUG-012 — MEDIUM — Maintenance mode is bypassed for ads-subdomain traffic
- **Location:** `NoName/settings.py:182-183`; `_.middleware.py:137-252`.
- **Evidence:** `AdsSubdomainMiddleware` returns responses directly for disallowed ads paths, all advert-subdomain pages, legacy promote redirects and 404s, so `MaintenanceModeMiddleware` never runs for them.
- **Impact:** Advert landing pages stay live during planned downtime.
- **Fix:** Reorder middleware so maintenance runs first, or apply the same maintenance check at the top of `AdsSubdomainMiddleware`.

#### BUG-013 — MEDIUM — Blank `SiteSettings` fields do not fall back as documented
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/config.py:78-103`; `ADMIN/models.py:46-52`; `NoName/settings.py:205-210` (global context processor).
- **Evidence:** `get_solo()` uses `get_or_create(pk=1)`; the config comment promises fallback to `About` defaults when fields are blank, but only `tweeter` uses `or About.tweeter`. A freshly created empty row yields empty social/contact links. The first render or even a 404 (`HOME/views.py:159-162`) can write the row.
- **Impact:** Broken footer/contact links; write-on-read in 404/email paths; indefinite cache lifetime.
- **Fix:** Create the singleton in a data migration, use `get()` with safe defaults, apply `or About.<field>` to every field, and give the cache a finite TTL.

#### BUG-014 — MEDIUM — Hardcoded/invalid contact and alert addresses
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/config.py:30,33` (`contact_email`/`email` are `@shaefalaap.resend.app`, i.e. missing a local part); `NoName/settings.py:44,333`; `SERVICE_INTERNAL/email_single.py:97`; `AUTHENTICATION/templates/auth/password_reset.html:101`.
- **Evidence:** Password reset page renders `mailto:@shaefalaap.resend.app`; security/archive alerts fall back to personal-looking addresses when env vars are absent.
- **Impact:** Broken support contact link; misdirected security/archive notifications; brand inconsistency.
- **Fix:** Source public contact addresses from validated `SiteSettings`/env, use `security@<domain>` defaults, and fail fast in production for required addresses.

#### BUG-015 — MEDIUM — External DB configuration uses truthy strings and forced SSL
- **Location:** `NoName/settings.py:217-227`.
- **Evidence:** `if os.getenv('use_external'):` treats `"False"`/`"0"` as true; `dj_database_url.config(...)` can raise if no URL is set; `OPTIONS` is overwritten with `{"sslmode": "require"}`.
- **Impact:** Accidental external DB selection, opaque startup crash, connection failures for non-SSL Postgres.
- **Fix:** Strict boolean parsing, explicit error for missing URL, merge rather than replace options, make `sslmode` configurable.

#### BUG-016 — MEDIUM — Upload validation trusts client metadata; no landing-page size cap
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/images.py:102-116,310-325,382-415`; `NoName/settings.py:317`.
- **Evidence:** Image validation checks only client-supplied `content_type`/size (no magic bytes); the error text mentions only JPEG/PNG although WEBP is allowed at `images.py:46`; `fetch_advert_landing_html()` reads the whole raw object into memory despite `ADVERT_LANDING_MAX_BYTES` being configured; archive validation trusts the original filename extension.
- **Impact:** Mislabeled/malicious content can reach Cloudinary; oversized raw pages can spike memory/latency; misleading errors.
- **Fix:** Validate real file signatures, stream with a byte cap, fix the error message, set safe content types/disposition.

#### BUG-017 — LOW — Dead `handler404` in `_/urls.py` returns 200
- **Location:** `_.urls.py:10-11`. Root handler is correctly set at `NoName/urls.py:27`, so this one is unused.
- **Fix:** Remove it, or pass `status=404`.

#### BUG-018 — LOW — `About.domain` uses raw `ALLOWED_HOSTS[0]`
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/config.py:19-22`; compare `SERVICE_INTERNAL/hosts.py:68-74` which already skips wildcards.
- **Evidence:** `ALLOWED_HOSTS=['.example.com','example.com']` produces `About.domain == 'https://.example.com'`.
- **Impact:** Broken canonical tags, social previews, JSON-LD and sitemap entries.
- **Fix:** Use `canonical_origin()`.

#### BUG-019 — LOW — Manual `?v=` cache busters with hashed static storage
- **Location:** `HOME/templates/base.html:70-71,111-116`; `HOME/templates/HOME/promote.html:19,446`; `NoName/settings.py:273-277`.
- **Impact:** Redundant cache variants and hand-maintained versions that can drift from the manifest hash.
- **Fix:** Rely on `CompressedManifestStaticFilesStorage`; keep manual versioning only for external assets.

#### BUG-020 — LOW — No fail-fast validation for `DJANGO_SECRET`
- **Location:** `NoName/settings.py:16`; `.env:1`.
- **Fix:** Raise `ImproperlyConfigured` when the variable is missing in production.

