### 3.5 Frontend JavaScript and templates

#### BUG-047 — HIGH — Stored XSS in AJAX comment insertion
- **Location:** `HOME/static/home/js/interactions.js:1765-1769` (sink); `BLOG/views.py:1772-1793` (source).
- **Evidence:** `CommentCreateView` stores the raw trimmed comment and returns it unchanged as `content` in the AJAX `JsonResponse` (`BLOG/views.py:1793`). The client builds the new comment with `article.innerHTML = … '<p>' + (payload.content || value) + '</p>'` (`interactions.js:1768`). A comment `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` executes immediately. A page reload does **not** execute it because `BLOG/templates/blog/story_detail.html:314` autoescapes the stored value, confirming the sink is the AJAX path.
- **Impact:** Any signed-in commenter can run same-origin script in the browser of readers who see the fresh comment, including admin sessions — session-riding, DOM defacement and data exfiltration.
- **Fix:** Build the body paragraph as a DOM node and set `textContent`; never concatenate comment text into `innerHTML`.

#### BUG-048 — HIGH — Stored XSS from story heading in the analytics search fragment
- **Location:** `ADMIN/templates/ADMIN/partials/analytics_story_search.html:13` (source); `ADMIN/static/control/js/analytics.js:932` (sink).
- **Evidence:** Django escapes the heading into `data-story-title`, but `getAttribute()` decodes it; `analytics.js:932` then writes `chosen.innerHTML = "Showing <strong>" + button.getAttribute("data-story-title") + "</strong>"`. A heading such as `</strong><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` breaks out and executes when an admin clicks the search result.
- **Impact:** Stored script execution in the admin surface with the admin's origin privileges and CSRF token.
- **Fix:** Use `textContent` and append a `<strong>` text node, or escape the decoded attribute before any `innerHTML` assignment.

#### BUG-049 — HIGH — Stored XSS in profile/admin JSON pager rendering
- **Location:** `HOME/static/home/js/interactions.js:1158-1203` (renderer), `:1469` (`list.innerHTML = …`); `HOME/views.py:2949-2956` and `ADMIN/views.py:257-265` (raw JSON fields); live pagers at `HOME/templates/HOME/profile.html:498-518` and `ADMIN/templates/ADMIN/staff_detail.html:267-287`.
- **Evidence:** `renderProfileItems()` concatenates attacker-influenced `item.heading`, `item.excerpt`/`detail`, `item.url`, `item.edit_url` and `item.blog_id` into an HTML string without escaping (`:1182`, `:1193`, `:1196`, `:1201`). Clicking page 2 replaces the server-escaped DOM with this unsafe HTML.
- **Impact:** Stored script execution on profile and admin pages; the admin variant can reach protected endpoints with admin privileges.
- **Fix:** Build list items with DOM nodes and `textContent`, or add and consistently apply `escapeHtml`/`escapeAttr` to every interpolated field and validate URLs before putting them in `href`.

#### BUG-050 — MEDIUM — Hero carousel double-advances on touch devices
- **Location:** `HOME/static/home/js/carousel.js:65-83` (pointer handlers) and `:93-108` (touch handlers).
- **Evidence:** Both handler pairs call `next()`/`prev()` and `start()` for the same swipe. On touch browsers `pointerdown`/`pointerup` and `touchstart`/`touchend` both fire, so a >60px swipe advances twice (pointer threshold 60, touch threshold 50). `suppressClick` only blocks the synthetic link click.
- **Impact:** A single mobile swipe skips a featured story and restarts autoplay twice.
- **Fix:** Use Pointer Events only, or register the touch handlers only when `window.PointerEvent` is unavailable / add a shared gesture guard.

#### BUG-051 — MEDIUM — Edit-page inline-image preview differs from published markup
- **Location:** `HOME/static/home/js/edit-news-editor.js:308-312,339-343`; correct add-page renderer `HOME/static/home/js/add-news-editor.js:1027-1041`; server renderer `BLOG/views.py:623-670`.
- **Evidence:** The edit preview renders a bare `<img class="story-inline-img story-inline-img-*">` and treats trailing token text only as `alt`; the published/add path renders `<figure class="story-inline-fig story-inline-fig-*">` with `<figcaption>`. `HOME/static/home/css/base.css:1424` documents that the plain rules exist only for the edit preview.
- **Impact:** Authors see a preview that does not match the published article: captions, framing, sizing and accessibility semantics differ.
- **Fix:** Port `renderInlineImage()` from `add-news-editor.js` and align the class map and caption handling with `BLOG/views.py`.

#### BUG-052 — LOW — Auth-gate fallback message is ignored
- **Location:** `HOME/static/home/js/interactions.js:215-220`; `HOME/static/home/js/auth-gate.js:80-84`.
- **Evidence:** `openAuthGate(kind, fallbackMessage)` passes only `kind` to `window.AbuAuthGate.open()`; `AbuAuthGate.open(kind)` accepts no message. Server-specific 401 details are discarded. One call site passes the placeholder `"GGGGGGGGGGGGGG."` as its fallback.
- **Impact:** Contextual sign-in reasons are lost; an unfinished placeholder can appear if the gate script fails to load.
- **Fix:** Extend `AbuAuthGate.open()` to accept and render the message with `textContent`, or remove the dead parameter and placeholders.

#### BUG-053 — LOW — Several cache-buster versions predate their asset changes
- **Location:** `HOME/templates/base.html:112-113,116` (`app.js`, `carousel.js`, `auth-gate.js` at `?v=20261016-1`); `HOME/templates/HOME/home.html:274` (`continue-popup.js?v=20261012-1`); `ADMIN/templates/ADMIN/panel.html:10,544` (`panel.css`/`panel.js` at `?v=20261110-2`).
- **Evidence:** Read-only `git log` dates for the referenced files are 2026-11-02, 2026-10-27, 2026-11-05, 2026-11-05 and 2026-11-19 respectively — all later than the embedded version. Related to BUG-019.
- **Impact:** Returning browsers/CDN edges may keep executing stale JS/CSS after deployment.
- **Fix:** Bump the versions to at least the last change date/hash, or drop manual query strings in favour of hashed static filenames and add a CI check.

