### 3.7 Blog and archive content

#### BUG-060 — HIGH — Stored XSS via `javascript:` URLs in `filel` / `btn` story tokens
- **Location:** `BLOG/views.py:88-98` (`tag_outbound_url`), `:690-698` (`_render_inline_file`), `:712-719` (`_render_inline_button`); preview-only guard at `:497-509`; `BLOG/tests.py:232-236`.
- **Evidence:** `tag_outbound_url()` deliberately returns non-http(s) URLs unchanged. The file and button renderers only `html.escape()` that value before placing it in `href`. A read-only render of `filel javascript:alert(1) Bad file` produced `<a class="story-inline-file" href="javascript:alert(1)" …>`, and `btn javascript:alert(document.domain) Click me` produced an executable button anchor. The existing test checks only that no `<iframe>` preview is created.
- **Impact:** A story authoring account (or pasted untrusted content) can plant click-triggered same-origin script execution for readers.
- **Fix:** Add a single `safe_href()` helper used by every author-supplied anchor renderer; allow only http/https (and relative paths/mailto/tel where intended), reject `javascript:`, `data:`, `vbscript:`, backslashes and control characters. Add tests asserting no `href="javascript:` for both tokens.

#### BUG-061 — HIGH — “Only me” archive files remain public Cloudinary assets
- **Location:** `SERVICE_INTERNAL/images.py:139-146,443-448,503-509,549-563` (uploads/destroy use default public delivery); `ARCHIVE/views.py:1163-1203` (proxy redirects owner to the raw public URL); contrast signed/authenticated advert landing handling at `images.py:262-266,300-302,334-337`.
- **Evidence:** `visibility=private` is enforced only by the Django `/archive/cdn/` proxy. On owner access the view issues `HttpResponseRedirect(real_url)` to a plain public Cloudinary URL; anyone with that URL (history, referrer, shared link, guessed public ID) can fetch the bytes without Django.
- **Impact:** “Only me” is not a privacy boundary; private photos/files are publicly accessible at the storage layer.
- **Fix:** Upload private archive assets with `type="authenticated"` (or `private`), generate per-request signed delivery URLs in the proxy, pass the same `type=` to `destroy_archive_asset()`, migrate existing private rows and add tests that the redirected target is signed and unsigned access fails.

#### BUG-062 — MEDIUM — Stale htmx pages cause 404s on gallery/manage pagination POSTs
- **Location:** `ARCHIVE/views.py:510-511,589-590` (`_paginate`/`_paginate_own` raise Http404), `:619-635` (GET catches it), `:637-648` (POST does not), `:838-859` (manage modal/list do not).
- **Evidence:** The gallery docstring promises a stale page falls back to page 1, but only `get()` wraps `_paginate()` in `try/except Http404`. htmx pager POSTs send the current `page`; after filtering reduces the result set, the next POST raises 404 and replaces the grid with an error.
- **Impact:** Broken gallery/manage UI instead of a corrected first page.
- **Fix:** Put the fallback inside `_paginate()`/`_paginate_own()` or wrap every GET and POST caller, preserving filters while resetting only `page`.

#### BUG-063 — MEDIUM — “Unknown” uploader filter only filters one hibernated account
- **Location:** `ARCHIVE/views.py:377-386` (`_clean_uploader` accepts only a digit PK), `:389-409` (`_uploader_options` collapses hibernated uploaders into one option tied to the first PK), `:419-432`, `:623-634`.
- **Evidence:** All hibernated uploaders are shown as a single “Unknown” option whose `pk` is the first one encountered; selecting it filters by that one `author_id`.
- **Impact:** Users cannot find uploads from all anonymized accounts; result counts and filter chips are misleading.
- **Fix:** Use an explicit `uploader=unknown` sentinel and filter `author__deleted_at__isnull=False` across paginating/ranking helpers.

#### BUG-064 — MEDIUM — Story cache keeps stale author profile data
- **Location:** `BLOG/views.py:1198` (100s cache with `select_related("author__staffprofile")`), `:1227-1231` (refreshes only `Auth` fields and pops `author_name`), `:1246-1247`, `:1378-1402` (JSON-LD author data); `BLOG/signals.py:37-45`; `STAFF/signals.py:12-17`; `HOME/views.py:1643-1649`. Expands BUG-034.
- **Evidence:** The cached reverse `staffprofile` object is not refreshed, so `full_name`, `slug`, `bio`, `role`, `speciality` and socials remain stale on the story page and structured data until TTL expiry. Hibernation is partly protected by the `deleted_at` refresh, but the Redis bulk key cleanup is ineffective (BUG-034).
- **Impact:** Wrong byline, stale bio/social/portfolio URLs and stale SEO metadata; possible 404 links.
- **Fix:** Invalidate `blog-<slug>` whenever `StaffProfile` or the Blog row changes (Redis-aware pattern delete for hibernation), or fetch the profile fresh in `StoryDetailView`.

#### BUG-065 — MEDIUM — Sitemap and feeds advertise story URLs that render 404
- **Location:** `BLOG/views.py:1251-1255` (story returns 404 when author has no `StaffProfile`); `HOME/sitemap_views.py:32-39,88-90,117-119`; `HOME/views.py:372-377` (RSS/Atom).
- **Evidence:** Sitemap/feed querysets filter on slug only; the story view applies an additional `StaffProfile` visibility rule. There is no shared “published/visible” queryset.
- **Impact:** Search engines and feed readers receive URLs that 404; crawl budget and index quality suffer.
- **Fix:** Introduce one canonical `published_stories()` queryset used by the story page, sitemap, feeds and 404 suggestions; at minimum add `.filter(author__staffprofile__isnull=False)` to sitemap/feed queries.

#### BUG-066 — LOW — Visible debug `<hr>` rules in story pages
- **Location:** `BLOG/templates/blog/story_detail.html:194` (`color:red;height:4px`) and `:386` (`color:var(--ink);height:4px`).
- **Impact:** Leftover debug separators make every story page look unfinished.
- **Fix:** Remove them or replace with a semantic CSS class.

#### BUG-067 — LOW — Category recommendation images bypass the same-origin CDN proxy
- **Location:** `BLOG/views.py:1576` (returns `story.image_1` raw); `BLOG/static/blog/js/category-recommendations.js:76` (assigns directly to `img.src`); contrast `BLOG/templates/blog/story_detail.html:413` uses `{{ story.image_1|cloudinary_proxy }}`.
- **Impact:** Inconsistent asset policy, possible CSP/referrer issues, and breakage if an image is ever moved to authenticated delivery.
